## Completion evidence (2026-10-15)

The command router now exposes `executeIssue(runId, issueId)` for bounded execution and integration through the existing fake OpenCode HTTP adapter and real Git worktrees. Initial execution and two repairs share one issue ledger, reserved before submission setup. Executor/merger deadline failures, setup failures and failed validation consume that budget. History preserves correlated results, logs, conflict feedback and saved work references. Retry cancels owned activity and reconciles retained branch/HEAD/dirty facts. Exhausted issues remain inspectable and repeated/concurrent calls cannot create an automatic fourth job. Permission denial and cancellation wait without fabricated repairs.

Candidate validation reuses baseline run-local skips across repairs and subsequent validation. Only actual validation timeouts with confirmed tree cleanup add skips. All-skipped validation integrates with `passed_with_omissions`, disclosed with issue attempts in status. New runs retry the original checks; configuration stays byte-for-byte unchanged. Setup timeout, spawn error, setup failure, nonzero exit, denial and cancellation remain distinct; cleanup is never skipped. Live process ownership is persisted during command execution so stop can kill a running check without labelling it timed out. `agentTimeoutMs` is visible in project configuration/run settings/attempt status with a thirty-minute default; tests inject a controllable clock.

